---
// /data-deletion: Meta's Data Deletion Instructions URL for the Wren app's
// connected accounts (wren designs/2026-10-09-app-reviews.md). Keep in step with
// /privacy "The Wren app".
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro';
import Foot from '../components/Foot.astro';
const site = (await getEntry('site', 'site'))!.data;
const updated = 'October 9, 2026';
---
<Base title="Data deletion | Wren Automation" description="How to remove the Wren app's access to an account and have what it read deleted." hue="lavender">
<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="nav" aria-label="Page">
    <a href="/" aria-label="Wren Automation, front page"><Mark /></a>
    <div class="right">
      <button class="theme" type="button" data-theme-toggle data-to-dark={site.theme.to_dark} data-to-light={site.theme.to_light} aria-label="Switch between light and dark">{site.theme.to_dark}</button>
    </div>
  </nav>
</div>
<main>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Data deletion</h1>
    <p class="lede">How to remove the Wren app's access to an account you connected, and have what it read deleted. Last updated {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="s">
  <div class="wrap legal">
    <h2>Remove access</h2>
    <p>In Wren, go to Account, then Social, and press Disconnect next to the account. The access token is deleted right away and the app stops reading the account.</p>
    <p>You can also do it from the platform's side:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Facebook: Settings, then Business integrations. Remove Wren.</li>
      <li>Instagram: Settings, then Apps and websites. Remove Wren.</li>
      <li>Google and YouTube: <a href="https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions">security.google.com/settings/security/permissions</a>. Remove Wren.</li>
      <li>TikTok: Settings and privacy, then Security, then Apps and services. Remove Wren.</li>
      <li>LinkedIn: Settings, then Data privacy, then Permitted services. Remove Wren.</li>
      <li>X: Settings, then Security and account access, then Apps and sessions. Revoke Wren.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Delete what the app read</h2>
    <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> from the address on your Wren login or on the connected account, and say which account. Within 30 days I delete everything the app read from it (posts, their numbers, comments, messages, reviews) along with the connection, and I email you when it's done. Records a business has to keep by law, like invoices, stay only as long as the law requires.</p>
    <p>The rest of what Wren Automation collects is on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<Foot site={site} />
</Base>
